\import{base-macros}

\p{Continues [rep-truffle-T2](rep-truffle-T2) (what the tier is, its deviations from ISA 8.4, its correctness record). This file: the measurements T2 could not take, what the tier costs and gains on each platform and why, what was changed, and the go / no-go. Scratch, scripts, logs and raw rows: \code{\verb~|work/t3/~} (\code{\verb~|warm.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|logs/~}). Section 10 is the second task of the same day: the prototype of U1, the CALL instruction (NO-GO).}

\subtree{
\title{1. Verdict: NO-GO as a default; what the tier is worth, and under which policy}

\p{\strong{The Truffle tier does not pay on Cedar-level work and cannot under the present value model; on closed evaluation (reachability) it is worth 4 - 5\% of the warm wall clock in the native image and 7 - 10\% on the JVM, with a promotion policy that compiles only the dozen blocks that carry the run. On the Cedar slice it is neutral in the image and a loss on the JVM. \code{\verb~|t2~} stays off by default.} Nothing here argues for switching it on in the launcher. Nothing argues for deleting it either: it is correct (section 8), and it is the place where U1 / U2 of section 7 would pay.}

\p{Warm wall clock per pass in ms: median of the later half of the warm passes of all runs of the configuration in the window (in brackets, where it matters, the range of those passes). \code{\verb~|K1~} = \code{\verb~|default,code,casetrees~}; tier = the same + \code{\verb~|t2~}, \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.t2.mode=warm~}, without the rejected run-ahead. Every row is one \src{bench/quiet.py} window, K1 and tier back to back on the same distribution (\code{\verb~|work/t3/warm.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|launcher.tsv~}; labels in the tables).}

\p{\strong{Table A - the final tree and the final policy} (promotion at 20000 entries and 2\% of all activations; fixes C7 / C8 of section 4 in; machine jar \code{\verb~|8a8ea5644b24~}):}

\table{
