\p{Not covered: the native image under a differential gate (the images \code{\verb~|work/t3/n2~}, \code{\verb~|n3~}, \code{\verb~|n5~} are the measuring tool only; no \code{\verb~|bin/rlvm~} of this tree was built); \code{\verb~|tele~} blocks under the production promotion; 8 workers under the equivalence test (it is single-session by construction; the launcher gate ran with 4 threads).}

\p{A defect of the test tooling found on the way (not of the tier): with background compilation, a second engine in the same process got nothing compiled, because the compiler threads were still working through the first engine's queue (T2's \code{\verb~|perfTestsBackground~} printed "blocks compiled 0" for its second file on this tree, and so did the first equivalence run for the Cedar slice and Init - rows that proved nothing and are not in the table). \code{\verb~|T2Engine.retire()~} (called by \code{\verb~|Harness.close~}) cancels an engine's queued compilations; \code{\verb~|perfTestsWarmMode~} asserts that compiled code ran in each file.}
}

\subtree{
\title{9. Open points, requests, next step}

\ol{
\li{\strong{Most rows are \code{\verb~|WarmMain~}, not the launcher.} P7 published kept-engine passes at 18:04Z (\code{\verb~|-X passes-keep=engines~}); one launcher window was taken with them (L1: reachability and full cedar). The Cedar slice on the launcher was not steady in 7 passes; Init, Std and the native launcher were not run through it. No request of mine is open with anybody.}
\li{\strong{Not measured}: con-leche, cslib, mathlib, navier-stokes-euler; \code{\verb~|tele~} blocks under the tier in a timing run; the native image at Init / Std / full cedar; the launcher's native \code{\verb~|bin/rlvm~} with this tree (only the measuring tool was built as an image: \code{\verb~|work/t3/n5~} is the one of the final tree).}
\li{\strong{OPEN: why the Cedar slice on the JVM is 60 ms per pass slower with TWO compiled blocks} (J9: +4.3\% at one worker, +30\% at eight, CPU time of the workers unchanged at eight). What I know: the two blocks are \code{\verb~|RULE(List.rec)~} (5 instructions, the hottest block of reachability too, where it gains) and \code{\verb~|RULE(Bool.rec)~} (2 instructions), 45 k compiled activations per pass, compiled in 107 ms, 0 deoptimisations of the roots; it is not the retention of machines (C7) and not the report lock (C8): the row was +27\% before them. JFR of a slice run with 96 blocks (\code{\verb~|work/t3/jfr/t3-cedarslice.top.txt~}, open host): the hook's own frames (\code{\verb~|Tier.offer~} 1.0\%, \code{\verb~|T2Tier.run~} 0.5\%, \code{\verb~|OptimizedCallTarget.doInvoke~} 0.5\%) are about 2\% of the samples - the path \code{\verb~|Code.go -> Tier.exec -> Tier.offer -> T2Tier.run~} that EVERY activation takes once the switch is on, compiled or not - and the host's C2 compiler thread still has 9\% of the thread load in late passes. In the image the same workload is neutral with the same two blocks (N5) and +1.0\% with 88 (N3). So part of the one-worker figure may be the price of the hook on a workload with a million stepped activations per pass; the rest, and the 8-worker figure, is not explained. First things to try: the run with \code{\verb~|rlvm.t2.max=0~} on the final tree (the hook alone); \code{\verb~|-XX:+PrintCompilation~} for \code{\verb~|Code.resumeOne~} (the body that \code{\verb~|BUNREAD~} of \code{\verb~|RULE(List.rec)~} runs through; only the tier calls it, 45 k times per pass); the driver's per-unit times (\code{\verb~|-X unit-trace~}) for the unit on the critical path.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|rlvm.t2.inline=1~} against 0}: 1021 ms (two runs) against 974 (one run), reachability, JVM, window J3: no difference that the per-process variance (8\% between two K1 runs of that window) lets one see. Kept at 1 because it removes calls and never showed a loss; the image is built with 1.}
\li{\strong{The tier follows the machine by hand.} \code{\verb~|Instr.*~} mirrors \code{\verb~|Code.java~} statement by statement; the stepper answers \code{\verb~|KCONST~} of a level-polymorphic constant from the site's inline cache (NOTES-M7: "since wave 6"), T2's node did not (C3). The tier-equivalence tests do not see such a drift, because the values are the same. As long as \code{\verb~|rlvm-machine~} is republished every few minutes, an owner of this module has to diff \code{\verb~|Code.java~} against \code{\verb~|Instr.java~} before every measurement.}
\li{\strong{Internal API}: as NOTES-T2 section 7.8 (\code{\verb~|OptimizedCallTarget.compile / isValid / callIndirect / cancelCompilation~}, the compilation listener; the "no one-store setter, no one-call forwarder in compiled code" rule of native-image CE 25.5.5.0.3).}
}

\p{\strong{Next step, if anybody continues} (as written at 18:58Z): not more work inside this module. U1 of section 7 in the machine (a call instruction that does not build the redex; M7 / M3), measured in the stepper first - it should pay there by itself - and then direct calls between compiled blocks on top of it, which is the first point at which Truffle can do something the stepper cannot. \strong{Done in the second task (section 10): it does not pay there, and nothing is left for the tier on top of it.}}
}

\subtree{
\title{10. U1: the CALL instruction (second task, 19:00Z - 20:50Z): NO-GO in the stepper, nothing for \code{\verb~|t2~} on top}

\p{Proposed ISA section: \code{\verb~|work/t3/isa-call.md~} (design sections 1-8 written before the prototype, section 9 after it). Prototype: private tree \code{\verb~|work/t3/tree-call/tree~} (rlvm-machine + a copy of this module), switch \code{\verb~|call~} (bit 26, off by default); patches per owner in \code{\verb~|work/t3/patches-call/~} (README.txt there). Nothing of it is in the main tree and nothing in this module's sources.}

\subtree{
\title{10.1 Verdict}

\p{\strong{U1 is a NO-GO: the instruction is correct, gated, and worth nothing measurable} - in the stepper and in the Truffle tier, on the JVM and in the native image, on reachability and on Cedar-level work.}

\ul{
\li{The form I proposed (the application is never built: "form U") saves 1.9\% of reachability's records and costs 8.3\% more ticks and 21\% more block activations, because 77\% of the applications at CALL sites were answered by the WHNF memo of their record. On library corpora it saves 0.1-0.8\% of the records at equal ticks.}
\li{The form that keeps the application as the memo key ("form T", the prototype's default) changes no count by more than 0.3\% on any corpus.}
\li{Warm wall clock (bench/quiet.py, one engine kept; 10.4): \code{\verb~|call~} against the default set in twelve cells (JVM, launcher, image; reachability, Cedar slice, Init, Std, full cedar; 1 and 8 workers): between -4.5\% and +6.9\%, mean +0.4\%; in the steadiest cells (the image at one worker) it is 0.5-1.9\% slower.}
\li{For the tier there is nothing on top: \code{\verb~|t2~} and \code{\verb~|t2 + call~} are the same within the scatter, and the direct call node the task asked for was NOT built, because its object was counted first: 68 k calls per pass on reachability have a compiled caller and a compiled callee (4.5\% of the compiled activations), none on the Cedar slice (10.5).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{10.2 What was built}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Elaboration} (\code{\verb~|Elab~}, switch \code{\verb~|call~} only): the major premise of an inlined case tree whose term is an application of a definition becomes \code{\verb~|KCONST ; CALL r, h, args ; WHNF rM, r~} instead of \code{\verb~|KCONST ; MKAPP ; WHNF~}; an application of a definition in tail position becomes \code{\verb~|TAILAPPLY h, args~} instead of \code{\verb~|MKAPP ; RET~} (the same record at the same ticks in value mode).}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|CALLV~}} (\code{\verb~|Code.callLoop~}, shared by stepper and tier): one tick per head; the head's RULES block (case tree) or BODY block is entered directly on the arguments in scratch, in CALL MODE (marker in the window word of the captured frame); in call mode a \code{\verb~|TAILAPPLY~} of a constant hands head and arguments back (\code{\verb~|Op.TCALL~}) and the loop continues with the next head; over-application of a constant result is again a call; a suspended block leaves a frame \code{\verb~|K_CALL~} that re-enters the loop.}
\li{\strong{The generic path} (the application is built and the complete WHNF runs on it), exactly: head not a CONST record; head class not DEFN (constructors, axioms, opaque constants, recursors, Quot); a Nat function; a wrong number of levels or "does not unfold"; no RULES and no BODY block or fewer arguments than the block's arity; eager reduction active. Theorem heads are called (class DEFN); hints do not matter (CALL exists only where WHNF is asked; lazy delta keeps single DELTA steps on records); budgets are kept by the tick per iteration; K and literals are CORE's and NATFOLD's in the WHNF that follows.}
\li{\strong{Two forms} (a static of \code{\verb~|Code~}, one per JVM). Form U (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.t3.callUntabled=true~}): \code{\verb~|CALL~} is \code{\verb~|CALLV~}, the application exists only if the call is stuck. Form T (default): the application is interned first as the memo key; a WHNF flag or a WHNF memo answers; else \code{\verb~|CALLV~}, then the complete WHNF of its result, which is written into the application's WHNF memo (frames \code{\verb~|K_CALLT_1~}, \code{\verb~|K_CALLT_2~}).}
\li{\strong{Tier} (private copy of this module): \code{\verb~|Op.CALL~} is decoded like \code{\verb~|APPLY~}; \code{\verb~|Instr.Apply~} calls \code{\verb~|T2Bridge.callv~} (a boundary into \code{\verb~|Code.callTabled~} / \code{\verb~|Code.callv~}) and, for a \code{\verb~|TAILAPPLY~} of a constant in an activation in call mode, \code{\verb~|T2Bridge.tailCall~}. No direct call node (10.5).}
\li{\strong{Counters}: \code{\verb~|call.entered / memo / tail / builtAtSite / builtAfterTail~} (always), the census of block instructions and of record-table probes (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.t3.census=true~}), CALLs in compiled code and where the callee runs (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.t3.callCount=true~}); \code{\verb~|WarmMain~} prints them per pass.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{10.3 Counts per warm pass (one worker; off / form T / form U)}

\table{
\tr{\th{corpus}\th{ticks}\th{records built}\th{record-table probes}\th{block activations}\th{blocks entered by CALL / answered by the memo}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{9,095,141 / 9,094,072 / \strong{9,849,776 (+8.3\%)}}\td{4,819,810 / 4,818,323 / 4,727,624 (-1.9\%)}\td{8,369,951 / 8,391,415 / 8,650,323 (+3.4\%)}\td{1,755,468 / 1,755,477 / 2,128,006 (+21\%)}\td{T: 92,151 / 382,961; U: 464,637 / -}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{9,772,239 / 9,765,614 / 9,777,052}\td{5,031,495 / 5,029,993 / 5,025,412 (-0.12\%)}\td{10,924,782 / 10,923,479 / 10,920,964}\td{597,341 / 597,372 / 601,758}\td{T: 6,700 / 2,275; U: 9,197 / -}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{39,101,002 / 39,001,150 / 39,070,324}\td{16,194,242 / 16,154,662 (-0.24\%) / 16,080,771 (-0.70\%)}\td{33,213,640 / 33,175,585 / 33,117,125 (-0.29\%)}\td{4,310,644 / 4,312,342 / 4,347,413}\td{T: 106,605 / 29,626; U: 136,032 / -}}
